1 NAME Martin /Mortensen/
2 GIVN Martin
2 SURN Mortensen
2 _MARNM Mortensen
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Mare Island Cemetery 
2 ADDR
3 CITY Vallejo
3 STAE CA
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 8 FEB 1861
2 ADDR
3 CITY Stavanger
3 STAE Rogaland
3 CTRY Norway
1 BAPM
2 DATE 10 MAR 1861
2 PLAC St. Petri 
2 ADDR
3 CITY Stavanger
3 STAE Rogaland
3 CTRY Norway
1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 DEC 1901
2 ADDR
3 CITY Vallejo
3 STAE California
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Petty Officer, United States Navy
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/52607093?search=true
2 CONT
2 CONT Enlisted as seaman out of Norway & immigrated to US in 1880. Married Katie Higgins in 1894 in Vallejo, CA. 1900 census shows them living in Alameda where Mortensen was Petty Officer in US Navy at Alameda Naval Training Base. Died 
2 CONC of heart failure on Christmas day, 1901.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Mortensen-1065
2 CONT
2 CONT On 8 Feb 1861, Martin Mortensen was born in Stavanger, Rogaland, Norway to Morten Abrahamsen and Ingeborg Christine Aadnesdatter. Martin was baptised  on 10 March 1861. [1] https://urn.digitalarkivet.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20070105
2 CONC 310217.jpg (No 88, top row)
2 CONT
2 CONT At the time of the 1885 Minnesota state census, head of household Ole Mortenson (age 57, born in Norway) was living in Langhei, Minnesota with his wife Anne K. Mortenson (age 42, born in Norway), their son Marin Mortenson (age 24,
2 CONC  born in Norway), daughter Regine Mortenson (age 17, born in Norway), son Jens A. Mortenson (age 16, born in Norway), son Ole A. Mortenson (age 15, born in Norway), son Lars Ed Mortenson (age 9, born in MN), son Carl Albert Morten
2 CONC son (age 9, born in MN), son John G. Mortenson (age 5, born in MN), and son Edwin D. Mortenson (age 2, born in MN). [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 6 Jun 1900 at the time of the 1900 US census, head of household Martin Mortenson (age 39, born Feb 1861 in Norway) was employed as a Petty Officer in the US Navy and living in a home he rented at 5 Mastic Terrace in Alameda, Ca
2 CONC lifornia with his wife Katie Mortenson (age 29, born Jun 1871 in MO); son Earl Mortenson (age 5, born Aug 1895 in CA); and son Martin E. Mortenson (age 3, born Feb 1897 in CA). Martin and Katie had been married for 5 years. Katie 
2 CONC had given birth to two children, both of whom were still alive at that time. Both of Martin's parents were born in Norway; both of Katie's parents were born in Ireland. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death and Legacy
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin passed away in 1901.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fact: Burial Mare Island Cemetery , Vallejo, Solano County, California, USA
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT * "Norway Baptisms, 1634-1927," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:N7GB-SFX : 10 March 2018), Martin Mortensen, 08 Feb 1861; citing Domkirken, Stavanger, Rogaland, Norway; FHL microfilm 1,282,678.
2 CONT *"Minnesota State Census, 1885," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:MQXL-VXG : 4 August 2017), Martin Mortenson in household of Ole Mortenson, Langhei, Pope, Minnesota; citing p. 3, volume 
2 CONC Pope, State Library and Records Service, St.Paul; FHL microfilm 565,750.
2 CONT *"United States Census, 1900," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:M9P9-9WB : accessed 14 April 2019), Katie Mortenson in household of Martin Mortenson, Alameda Township, Precinct 11 Alameda
2 CONC  city, Alameda, California, United States; citing enumeration district (ED) 319, sheet 8B, family 198, NARA microfilm publication T623 (Washington, D.C.: National Archives and Records Administration, 1972.); FHL microfilm 1,240,08
2 CONC 1.
2 CONT *Martin Mortensen (1861-1901) on Find A Grave: Memorial #52607093 retrieved 03 December 2018
2 CONT *1900 census: Alameda Co CA Martin Mortensen b. Feb 1861 Norway, immigrated 1880, US Navy Petty Officer
