2 CONT RITES TODAY AT 2 FOR MRS. FUGLESTAD Funeral services for Mrs. T. T. Fuglestad, 96, will be at 2 this afternoon in Zion (Westley) Lutheran Church south of Cooperstown, the Rev. Sanford Soma officiating. Mrs. Fuglestad, one of Grigg
2 CONC s county’s pioneers, died Sunday at her home six miles southeast of Cooperstown. She leaves 99 descendants. Her husband died June 24, 1954, at the age of 98. Abigael Osland was born October 29, 1859 in Norway. She was married to M
2 CONC r. Fuglestad June 15, 1880, and they came to America in 1883. Their Atlantic crossing took three weeks. They spent their first winter in the sod home of a neighbor, building their home later in the spring. This sod house was built
2 CONC  about 20 feet from the present farm home. A few years later, Mr. Fuglestad cut and hauled logs from the Sheyenne river banks to build a log house. Surviving are four daughters, Mrs. Lars (Inga) Loge, Mrs. Swen (Lisa) Loge, and Mr
2 CONC s. Oswald (Gudrun) Aalgaard, Cooperstown and Mrs. R. (Thelma) Norheim, Pasadena, Calif., three sons, R. E. of Moorhead, Minn., Bjorn of Cooperstown and Thorvald of Luverne; 36 grandchildren and 56 great-grandchildren. Living at ho
2 CONC me with their mother were Bjorn Fuglestad and Mrs. Aalgaard. Pallbearers at the funeral will be six grandsons, Vernon, Torkel and Roald Fuglestad and Spencer, Maynard and Lawrence Loge. Published in the Griggs County Sentinel-Cour
2 CONC ier, Cooperstown, North Dakota, January 12, 1956.
2 CONT
