2 ADDR
1 OCCU Kasserer i Høyland Sparebank, eide gårdsbruk på Tjelta i Hetland, dreiv sildesalting i Stavanger.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Døde og begravede 1886, Høyland sokneprestkontor, AV/SAST-A-101799/001/30BA/L0011: Ministerialbok nr. A 10, 1878-1888, s. 223, Brukslenke for sidevisning: https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070103310220
2 CONT * Jæren Gards- og ættesoga, band II Høyland, Austvoll, side 101, nr. 38
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jæren Gards- og ættesoga, band II Høyland, Austvoll, side 101, nr. 38'''
2 CONT Jon Jakobson Hodnefjell, f. i Stavanger 16. okt. 1829, d. 23. jan. 1886, son til arbeidar Jakob Jonson Hodnefjell og Taletta Salomonsdtr. Bonde og kommunekasserar, kasserar i Høyland Sparebank, åtte gardsbruk på Tasta i Hetland, d
2 CONC reiv sildesalting i Stavanger.
2 CONT Gift 6. nov. 1849 med Karen Hallvardsdtr. Austvoll (23), f. 26. juli 1831, d. 28. april 1906.
2 CONT Born:
2 CONT * a. Hanne Kristine, f. 28. sept. 1850, d. 26. jan. 1896, gift 1) 5. des. 1867 med Andreas Knutson Kluge (Bd. I, Kluge 40. k), f. 12. des. 1837, d. 3. mai 1874, snikkar på Sandnes, og 2) 2. nov. 1876 med enkjemannen Jon Olson, f. 
2 CONC 17. jan. 1842, skipstømmermann i Stavanger.
2 CONT * b. Jakob (43).
2 CONT * c. Taletta, f. 2. april 1856, g. m. sjømann Laurits Jakobsen.
2 CONT * d. Hallvard (46).
2 CONT * e. Anna Gurine, g. m. Hans Larsson Soma (Soma 102).
2 CONT * f. Carl Johan, f. 19. mars 1863, d. 23. juli 1929, prest i Amerika, g. m. Ellen Sofie Nilsen, f. i U.S.A.
2 CONT * g. Jon, f. 28. des. 1865, gift i Amerika.
2 CONT * h. Andreas, f. 6. juli 1868, gift i Amerika.
2 CONT * i. Gustav Kornelius, f. 3. jan. 1872, gift i Amerika, d. 5. aug. 1947.
2 CONT * j. Karen Elisabet, g. m. Rasmus Johannesson Østvold (36. c).
2 CONT * k. Anna Olava, f. 23. febr. 1878, d. i Amerika 1. april 1927, ugift.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT John was called Østvold at the time of his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=6280&uid=ny&idx_side=-220
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Bonde og bankdirektør i Høyland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family lore states not only was he the director of the Hoyland Bank - as well as a farmer - but he also had some kind of fishing tackle business (nets, etc) in Sandness.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Farm (Ostvold, Austvoll, Eastvold Farm, Hoyland, Rogaland, Norway) Family history
2 CONT
2 CONT The farm family history goes back to 1693 and is run today by the 9th generation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hallvard Olsen from Grannes born in 1658, son of former sheriff of Jåtun Ship Reid, married the widow of the farm Dorotea Gabrielsdtr. Austrått that he got two girls with.Hallvard was widowed and remarried in 1719 with Berit Klaus
2 CONC dtr Skeiane, they got five girls grew up.
2 CONT
2 CONT From here starts the family bloodline on the farm. Hallvard Olsen spent from 1693 eighteen pounds in the yard Austvoll, where he owned a half pound yourself, rest leasehold land. He took the name Halvor Østvold.
2 CONT
2 CONT The eldest daughter Dorte Halvorsdtr. born in 1720 from the second marriage married Johannes Nilsson Heigre and they took over the farm when Halvor Østvold (Halvard Olsen) died in 1744. In 1743, John got Nilsson buy letter in half
2 CONC  the farm which was 6 container and leasehold 30 team. Dorte and John saw a boy and four girls grew up.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son Hallvard Johannessen born in 1746 married in 1764 with Karen Hallvardsdtr Helland and had 3 sons with her. Hallvard Johannessen was widowed and married again in 1792 with the widow Anna Olsdatter. Keys and got her four boys an
2 CONC d two girls.Hallvard Johannessen was freehold of 32 ½ pail. Here is a picture of the original document in a purchase contract from an auction in 1779. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1808 sold Hallvard Johannessen half of the farm to each of his sons Hallvard Hallvardsen and John Hallvardsen. The brothers lived with their families and parents in the same house "Tuptå" until the widow of John Hallvardsen rem
2 CONC arried and there was trouble between the families. Then they shared literally the house in 1842, Hallvard Hallvardsen got the southern part and the widow of John Hallvardsen the north part of the house. The houses were rebuilt in 
2 CONC their own yard.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hallvard Hallvardsen born in 1766 was married to Karen Jespersdtr. Nordland and had only one daughter, Karen born in 1831. Karen Hallvardsdtr. lost her father only three years old and her mother remarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Karen Hallvardsdtr. married 18 years with John Jakobsen Hodnefjell took over the farm. Besides being a farmer John Jakobsen was municipal treasurer and treasurer of Highland Savings Bank, he also owned a farm on Tasta and fis
2 CONC h sales organizations in Stavanger. Karen Hallvardsdtr. and John Jakobsen had 5 girls and 6 boys grow up, of which eight siblings traveled to America for the genus is greater in America than in Norway. It was the second eldest son
2 CONC  Halvor born in 1858 who took over the farm.
2 CONT
2 CONT Halvor Johnsen married in 1885 to Rebecca Ivarsdatter Soma Halvor was born in 1860, he was a bank manager in Highland Sparebank beside being a farmer. Their children are John, Ivar, Karen and Anna, both Anna and her mother died of
2 CONC  tuberculosis in 189? and Halvor was a widower for life. He was also a trip to America for a visit with his siblings.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1909 shared John and Ivar the farm, John built a new yard while Ivar keep the old and her father living on a result in itself. Ivar married Ragnhild Kittelsdtr Egeland and got the children Rebekah, Harald and Elin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald took over in 1948 married to Kathy Sekse from Hardanger, they live today in folgehuset in Klunghaugen on the farm. It is their youngest son Rune Austvoll and wife, Rita, who runs the farm (2017).
2 CONT
2 CONT Rita's blood line also goes back on the farm Austvoll, she descended from another daughter of Hallvard Olsen and Berit Klausdtr. called Berit born in 1729.
